1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Open with the extension icon.
Click Tab Station in Chrome to open your manager.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Your manager opens in one step.
Organize your real browser tabs.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Open Tab Station with a keyboard shortcut.
Mac: Command+Shift+E. Windows / Linux: Ctrl+Shift+E.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
All your tabs. One workspace.
Tab Station — organize the tabs you actually use.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
See every window
Manage real tabs across browser windows.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Find it instantly
Search open tabs by title or URL.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Preview before you clean up
See which duplicate tabs will stay or close.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Remove duplicate tabs
Pinned tabs take priority.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Save a page for later
Read later saves the page and closes its source tab.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Pick up where you left off
Opening a Read later item removes it from the list.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Save a browsing task
Keep a window snapshot for future use.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Restore your workspace
Saved windows can be reused.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Restore again whenever you need
Restoring a window keeps its saved snapshot.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Tab Station — Your tabs. In your hands.
Find, rearrange, and restore.
